{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E2gZSGnT14NDZAF7Xfvrpe","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/runbooks:\ngate-2.md\n\ninternal/cli:\napp.go\ncli_test.go\ncmd_config.go\ncmd_init.go\ncmd_labels.go\ncmd_rebuild.go\ncmd_serve.go\ncmd_version.go\nlog.go\nlog_test.go\nroot.go\nrun.go\n\ninternal/roles:\nconfig.yaml\ncve_docker_integration_test.go\ncve_integration_test.go\ncve_test.go\ndocs_docker_integration_test.go\ndocs_test.go\neng_review_test.go\nengineer_test.go\nerrcodes_integration_test.go\nerrcodes_test.go\nlead_test.go\nlicense_review_integration_test.go\nlicense_review_test.go\nlint_docker_integration_test.go\nlint_integration_test.go\nlint_scan_test.go\nlint_test.go\nmissing_tests_integration_test.go\nmissing_tests_test.go\npm_review_test.go\nreviewers\nroles.go\nroles_test.go\nscanner_guard_test.go\nscanners\nsecurity_review_test.go\ntestdata\ntriage\ntriage_roles_test.go\ntrufflehog_docker_integration_test.go\ntrufflehog_history_test.go\ntrufflehog_integration_test.go\ntrufflehog_test.go\nworker_engineer_test.go\nworkers\n// Command ard is the automated repository development controller.\n// See docs/proposal.md for the design.\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"os\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/cli\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/configcmd\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/initcmd\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/labels/labelsync\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/servecmd\"\n)\n\n// version is set at build time with -ldflags \"-X main.version=...\".\nvar version = \"dev\"\n\nfunc main() {\n\tos.Exit(run(os.Args[1:], os.Stdout, os.Stderr))\n}\n\nfunc run(args []string, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int {\n\treturn cli.Run(args, stdout, stderr, handlers(), version)\n}\n\n// handlers wires one function per subcommand. Each new command adds one\n// line here; a nil field runs the command as a \"not implemented\" stub.\nfunc handlers() cli.Handlers {\n\treturn cli.Handlers{\n\t\tConfigCheck:  configcmd.Check,\n\t\tServe:        servecmd.Serve,\n\t\tLabelsSync:   labelsync.Command,\n\t\tRebuildState: servecmd.RebuildState,\n\t\tInit:         initcmd.Init,\n\t}\n}\ninternal/cli/app.go:17:type Globals struct {\ninternal/cli/app.go:25:type Env struct {\ninternal/cli/app.go:33:type Handlers struct {\ninternal/cli/app.go:42:type ServeOpts struct {\ninternal/cli/app.go:48:type ConfigCheckOpts struct {\ninternal/cli/app.go:55:type InitOpts struct {\ninternal/cli/app.go:65:type ExitError struct {\ninternal/cli/app.go:70:func (e *ExitError) Error() string { return e.Err.Error() }\ninternal/cli/app.go:71:func (e *ExitError) Unwrap() error { return e.Err }\ninternal/cli/app.go:76:type App struct {\ninternal/cli/app.go:87:func (a *App) run(cmd *cobra.Command, h func(ctx context.Context, e *Env) error) error {\ninternal/cli/app.go:101:func notImpl(cmdPath, issue string) error {\ninternal/cli/cmd_config.go:9:func newConfig(app *App) *cobra.Command {\ninternal/cli/cmd_init.go:9:func newInit(app *App) *cobra.Command {\ninternal/cli/cmd_labels.go:9:func newLabels(app *App) *cobra.Command {\ninternal/cli/cmd_rebuild.go:9:func newRebuildState(app *App) *cobra.Command {\ninternal/cli/cmd_serve.go:9:func newServe(app *App) *cobra.Command {\ninternal/cli/cmd_version.go:9:func newVersion(app *App) *cobra.Command {\ninternal/cli/log.go:12:func NewLogger(level string, w io.Writer) (*slog.Logger, error) {\ninternal/cli/root.go:14:func NewRoot(app *App) *cobra.Command {\ninternal/cli/root.go:55:func (a *App) setup(cmd *cobra.Command) error {\ninternal/cli/root.go:73:func validateRepo(repo string) error {\ninternal/cli/run.go:17:func Run(args []string, stdout, stderr io.Writer, h Handlers, version string) int {\n40:  workers/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5, timeout: 60m, tests: make test }\n41-  reviewers/eng-review: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n# Layout\n\nEvery top-level directory and Go package, with what it holds. Keep it current: a PR that adds, removes or renames a directory or package updates this file in the same PR.\n\n```\ncmd/ard/                    CLI entry point; wire a new subcommand by adding one line to handlers()\ninternal/cli/               cobra command tree, global flags, slog logging; Handlers is the plug-in point\ninternal/botcheck/          tests for the bot-commit audit in .github/workflows/bot-commits.yml\ninternal/github/            GitHub client: domain types, Reader/Writer/Client, App auth, retry transport; query/ (search builder), fake/ (test double), clienttest/ (conformance suite)\ninternal/config/            .ard/config.yaml + role directory loading into a Resolved value (pure, fs.FS in)\ninternal/configcmd/         `ard config check` handler: prints the resolved config, returns validation errors; `--ref` checks a commit\ninternal/configsrc/         config from origin/main: a snapshot per SHA under ~/.ard/config/<owner>/<repo>/ (what `ard serve` reads)\ninternal/executor/          Executor interface and plain-data job types\ninternal/executor/local/    git worktree + host subprocess or docker run, watchdog, logs\ninternal/agent/             Adapter interface, Spec/Result types, Registry (pure: builds argv, parses output)\ninternal/agent/claude/      Claude Code adapter (`claude -p`, stream-json parser)\ninternal/modelauth/         picks the one model credential (OAuth token or API key) from the controller env and carries its value to the executor; never logged\ninternal/state/             SQLite controller and scanner state (sqlitex, scannerdb)\ninternal/scanner/           scanner pipeline: findings, markers, reconcile, diff, group, ExecEngine, the scanners Loop, rebuild\ninternal/costblock/         the issue body's ard-owned cost block: render, strict parse, strip (admission), splice, per-issue Locks; leaf, stdlib only\ninternal/costs/             the costs Loop: writes each dirty issue's cost table from state; Claims() false so it runs while paused\ninternal/scanner/stale/     the stale closer: a plain controller Loop that comments and closes untouched scanner issues\ninternal/agentjob/          helpers the agent loops share: untrusted-input snapshot, admission re-check, agent command and executor job builders, handle save, shutdown-aware wait, post-once\ninternal/worker/            the worker loop: claim, agent/test/fix steps, diff guard, code-lane push, draft PR, FinishWith\ninternal/servecmd/          `ard serve` and `ard rebuild-state`: dependency wiring (lock, state, effects, pool adoption, controller); registerLoops takes one line per loop\ninternal/redact/            log redaction (secrets and host paths), secret scan and 1 MiB cap (leaf library; close-out commits only LogResult.Clean)\ninternal/roles/             starter .ard/ tree (config.yaml, role dirs) embedded for ard init (scanners/cve, scanners/docs, scanners/error-codes, scanners/lint, scanners/missing-tests, scanners/trufflehog, scanners/trufflehog-history, triage/lead, triage/engineer, workers/engineer, reviewers/eng-review, reviewers/license-review, reviewers/security-review)\ninternal/pool/              slot arbiter for max_pods (stdlib only, no I/O): priority classes, per-issue triage cap\ninternal/effects/           the only writer: Effects interface, Live and DryRun (JSONL ledger), Open factory; archtest/ enforces \"only effects writes\"\ninternal/gitx/              git CLI wrapper (Commit, Push, StagedPaths, FileAt); gittest/ builds bare-repo fixtures; Commit/Push are for internal/effects only\nworkflows\n3:# Anything unset takes its built-in default (docs/proposal.md, Configuration).\n29:    # What builds, signs and deploys ard itself (docs/proposal.md, Delivery).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a253a109-e978-4c7d-84d8-99ab20ba9f29","uuid":"fa4e0391-b964-420b-ba47-0f25d60fbf38","timestamp":"2026-11-24T12:29:56.517Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"docs/runbooks:\ngate-2.md\n\ninternal/cli:\napp.go\ncli_test.go\ncmd_config.go\ncmd_in